*Proof:* Suppose \( f(a) = f(b) = t \). Then \( f(t + y) \mid (a + f(y)) \) and \( f(t + y) \mid (b + f(y)) \) imply \( f(t + y) \mid (a - b) \). Since \( y \) can be arbitrarily large, either \( f \) is bounded or \( a = b \).

**Case 1: \( f \) is injective.**
*Claim:* \( f(1) = 1 \).
