- If \( S = \{1, 2\} \), \( f(n) \) alternates between \( 1 \) and \( 2 \) for large \( n \). Then \( f(y + f(n)) \mid f(y) + n \) implies \( f(y + 1) = 1 \) for all \( y \). If \( f(n) = 1 \) for \( n > 1 \) odd and \( f(n) = 2 \) for \( n \) even, \( f(1) \) must be odd. If \( f(n) = 1 \) for \( n \) even and \( f(n) = 2 \) for \( n > 1 \) odd, a contradiction arises.

Thus, the solutions are as stated. <<<END>>
