From \( x > 0 > y \), \( x \leq 12.5 \), \( y \geq -12.5 \), and \( x - y \leq 20 \), it follows that:
$$
a_{10} \cdot a_{20} + a_{30} \cdot a_{40} \leq \frac{x^2 + y^2}{4} \leq 6.25^2 + 3.75^2.
$$
This is attainable when \( a_{10} = a_{20} = 6.25 \) and \( a_{30} = a_{40} = -3.75 \).
Therefore, the greatest possible value of \( a_{10} \cdot a_{20} + a_{30} \cdot a_{40} \) is:
$$
\boxed{6.25^2 + 3.75^2}.
$$
