\]
Since \(W(2,c) = \frac{|C|}{W(1,2)}\), we have:
\[
W(1,3) W(3,c) + \frac{|C|}{W(1,2)} W(3,c) = 2|C|.
\]
This simplifies to:
\[
\left(W(1,3) + \frac{|C|}{W(1,2)}\right) W(3,c) = 2|C|.
\]
For this to hold for all \(c \in C\), we must have \(W(1,3) = W(3,c) = \frac{2|C|}{W(1,2) + \frac{|C|}{W(1,2)}} = \frac{2|C| W(1,2)}{|C| + W(1,2)}\).

