In both cases, we have expressed \( A(x,y)z^2 + B(x,y)z + C(x,y) \) as a sum of two squares, proving the existence of polynomials \( F(x,y,z) \) and \( G(x,y,z) \) such that:
\[
F(x,y,z)^2 + G(x,y,z)^2 = A(x,y)z^2 + B(x,y)z + C(x,y).
\]

Thus, the proof is complete. <<<END>>
