  [14] We aim to find the smallest positive number \(\lambda\) such that for any complex numbers \(z_1, z_2, z_3 \in \{z \in \mathbb{C} \mid |z| < 1\}\) with \(z_1 + z_2 + z_3 = 0\) the following inequality holds
