   \[
   \{ f(af(a) + 1), f(af(a) - 1) \} = \{ af(f(a)) + 1, af(f(a)) - 1 \}.
   \]
   We get \( \{ 1, -1 \} = \{ af(f(a)) + 1, af(f(a)) - 1 \} \), so \( af(f(a)) = 0 \), which implies \( f(0) = 0 \).

3. **Case \( f(1) = 1 \):**  
