Notice that \( p_n > n \). Consider \( n = p_n - k_n \) for some \( k_n \in \mathbb{N} \).
In \( \mathbb{F}_{p_n} \), by Wilson's Theorem, we have:
$$
1 = (p_n - k_n)! = \frac{(p_n - 1)!}{(p_n - 1)(p_n - 2) \cdots (p_n - k_n + 1)} = \frac{-1}{(-1)^{k_n - 1} \cdot (k_n - 1)!} = (-1)^{k_n} \cdot \frac{1}{(k_n - 1)!}
$$
Thus,
$$
