\]
Noting \(4 \cos^2 \left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right) = 2 \cos \theta + 2\), we rewrite:
\[
[(2 \cos \theta + 2) x (1-x)] \cdot [1 - (2 \cos \theta + 2) x (1-x)].
\]
Letting \(t = (2 \cos \theta + 2) x (1-x)\), the above is \(t(1-t) \leq \frac{1}{4} < 2 - \sqrt{3}\), contradicting \(ABCD\) being a tapir. \(\blacksquare\)

