  [19] We claim that all integers \( k \neq 1 \) satisfy the desired property. First, recall that \(\frac{1}{n + 1} \binom{2n}{n}\) is the \( n \)-th Catalan number. Since the Catalan numbers are a sequence of integers, it follows that \( n + 1 \mid \binom{2n}{n} \) for all \( n \). Hence, \( k = 1 \) certainly cannot satisfy the problem statement.

