2. Applying this lemma to \( f(x) = x^n + ax^{n-1} + pq \) with \( p \) as a prime, if \( f(x) \) is reducible, it must have a rational root.
   Since \( f(x) \) is monic with integer coefficients, this rational root must be an integer.
3. Let \( r \) be an integer root of \( f(x) \). Then:
   \[
   r^n + ar^{n-1} + pq = 0 \implies pq = -r^n - ar^{n-1}.
