If \( m = 1000 \), each column has exactly one colored square, leaving no room for the remaining 999 squares, which is a contradiction. If \( m = 999 \), each of the 1000 rows has exactly one colored square, again leaving no room for the remaining 999 squares, which is also a contradiction. Hence, \( n = 1999 \) is the minimal value.
